{
 "about": "The looks for Movement I. A look is applied after the per-shot correction (grade/shots.json). Controls: 'curve' is display code value in -> out, a monotone cubic through the points (every look keeps 0 at 0, so picture black matches the matte and the title card, and holds 0.18-0.35, where dark skin sits); 'hue_keep' blends the per-channel curve (0) with a curve on the largest channel (1), which holds hue; 'neutral' pulls near-neutral pixels toward white: 'keep' is how much of their chroma survives, 'below'/'above' the saturation (max-min)/(max+0.08) where that is fully on / fully off, so skin and accents are not touched; 'saturation' is for everything that is not near-neutral; 'tint' is added to the neutrals by tonal zone ('reach' is the share that also reaches skin); 'accents' are the pushes on the three keyed accents (sat, hue_deg toward yellow, gain; lift_gamma/lift_below lift the wine); 'haze' and 'deepen_gain' scale the per-shot shaping; 'grain' is added once. 'accent_keys' are the keys themselves (hue range in degrees, the saturation and value ramps, 'soften' = blur passes on the key), measured on the matched picture. 'board' lists the look board's moments (seconds in the v4 cut).",
